{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Custom State and Traits","anchor":"Custom-State-and-Traits","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GlobalValue","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StateValue","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TraitKey"],"generated":true}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomStateAndTraits","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/customstateandtraits"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Custom State and Traits","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Carry your own data on entities and in globals, alongside the engine’s closed core.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The engine only ever branches on a closed set of traits and scalar globals, and that is what keeps its behavior auditable: every decision it can make is visible in a handful of small enums. Your game’s own data does not have to live in that set. A wallet, a set of combat stats, an item’s price — custom state and custom traits ride along type-erased through the same storage the engine already saves and restores, read by your rules and by nothing else.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Rich-Global-state","text":"Rich `@Global` state","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable & Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type can be a global. Conform it to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GlobalValue","type":"reference"},{"text":" with an empty conformance — the default implementation JSON-boxes it into the type-erased ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StateValue\/data(typeName:bytes:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" case, so there’s nothing to hand-pack:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct Purse: Codable, Sendable, GlobalValue {","    var coins: Int","    var receipts: [String] = []","}","","struct MyGame: Game {","    @Global var purse = Purse(coins: 10)","    \/\/ …","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Read and write it in rules exactly like a scalar global — it participates in the turn’s commit and in save\/restore through the one world-state funnel:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["lantern.before(.buy) {","    guard purse.coins >= 5 else { try refuse(\"You can't afford it.\") }","    purse.coins -= 5","    try reply(\"Sold. You have \\(purse.coins) coins left.\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The type needs only ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — not ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The boxed bytes are what participate in the world state’s equality and hashing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Those bytes are the reason to touch a struct global once per rule body rather than field by field. Reading one decodes and writing one encodes, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"purse.coins -= 5","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a decode, a mutate and an encode — fine on its own, but a rule that sets four fields pays for four round trips and, worse, loses an update if a nested expression writes the same global between the read and the write. Read it into a local, mutate the local, and assign it back once:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var wallet = purse","wallet.coins -= 5","wallet.receipts.append(\"lantern\")","purse = wallet"],"type":"codeListing"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A custom global is stored as opaque bytes, so if you change its shape, an old save may no longer decode — and a stored value that fails to decode is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fatalError"},{"text":", not a fall back to the declared default. (The default is only reached when the global’s ID is ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"absent"}]},{"text":" from the save, which is what happens when you add a whole new global.) Save validation cannot catch it first: it checks only that a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"text":" case is still a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"text":" case, and one payload looks like another. So keep custom state structs additive and optional-tolerant — new fields with defaults, and a hand-written ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(from:)"},{"text":" that keeps the default when a field won’t decode. Versioned codecs are a later effort.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note","style":"note","type":"aside"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Custom-traits","text":"Custom traits","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare a typed key once, then use it to declare a custom property inside an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Item { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Location { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block with ","type":"text"},{"code":"trait(_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The value is boxed with the same rule as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a scalar or a whole struct both work:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["extension TraitKey<Int> { static let price = Self(\"price\") }","extension TraitKey<String> { static let region = Self(\"region\") }","","let lantern = Item {","    name(\"brass lantern\")","    trait(.price, 5)","}","","let docks = Location {","    name(\"The Docks\")","    trait(.region, \"waterfront\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Read it back on the live proxy with the typed subscript, which returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the trait is absent or stored as a different type:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let price = lantern[.price] ?? 0"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A key declared with a default (","type":"text"},{"code":"TraitKey(\"weight\", default: 1)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") can be read as a non-optional ","type":"text"},{"code":"V","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" through ","type":"text"},{"code":"item[default: .weight]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Custom traits are ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"immutable declared facts","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — they never touch the world state. For per-entity state that ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"changes","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" during play (an item’s current charge, a creature’s HP), use a ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keyed however your system needs; traits are for the fixed properties an entity is born with.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Worked-example","text":"Worked example","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Lighthouse","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" example (","type":"text"},{"code":"Sources\/Lighthouse\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") keeps two ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s — ","type":"text"},{"code":"tideStage","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", bumped by a daemon and read by a room’s live description, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"keeperGreeted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", flipped by a dialogue rule — a compact look at custom state driving prose and branching.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Tests\/GnustoTests\/Support\/CustomStateGames.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" builds ","type":"text"},{"code":"ShopGame","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Purse","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" struct held in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a lantern with a ","type":"text"},{"code":"trait(.price, 5)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and a game-defined ","type":"text"},{"code":"buy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" verb whose rule reads the price and debits the purse — the commerce plugin in miniature. ","type":"text"},{"code":"CustomStateTests","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" boots it and confirms the struct global round-trips through save\/restore, the custom trait reads back through the typed subscript, and absent\/wrong-type reads return ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"See-also","text":"See also","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","type":"reference","isActive":true}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Plugins","type":"reference","isActive":true}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global","type":"reference","isActive":true}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GlobalValue","type":"reference","isActive":true}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Plugins":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Package a reusable game system as an importable unit of verbs and rules.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Plugins","title":"Plugins","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/plugins","role":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Global":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Global","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Global","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Custom game state with the same ergonomics as built-in state:"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/global","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Global","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GlobalValue":{"abstract":[{"text":"Types usable with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property wrapper.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GlobalValue","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GlobalValue","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GlobalValue","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"GlobalValue","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/globalvalue","role":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TraitKey":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/traitkey","type":"topic","title":"TraitKey","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TraitKey","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A typed handle for a custom trait, replacing the stringly-typed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"trait(\"price\", 5)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"item.trait(\"price\", as: Int.self)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pair with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"single declaration that carries its own value type:","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TraitKey","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TraitKey"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/WritingRules":{"role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","title":"Writing Rules","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Attach game logic to items, locations, and the world."}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/writingrules"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/StateValue":{"abstract":[{"text":"A value that can live in ","type":"text"},{"code":"WorldState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s global storage. The scalar cases","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each pair with a dedicated ","type":"text"},{"code":"GlobalValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StateValue\/data(typeName:bytes:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is the type-erased case that carries any other ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value, so custom","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state structs and custom traits need no new case of their own.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StateValue","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"StateValue"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StateValue","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"StateValue","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/statevalue","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto":{"role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An engine for writing interactive fiction in Swift."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","kind":"symbol","title":"Gnusto","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/StateValue/data(typeName:bytes:)":{"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StateValue\/data(typeName:bytes:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"data","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"typeName","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"bytes","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4DataV","text":"Data","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"title":"StateValue.data(typeName:bytes:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/statevalue\/data(typename:bytes:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"}}}